sequenceDiagram
    participant AR as Alice<br/>lanlink-client-reader
    participant AS as Alice<br/>lanlink-file-sender
    participant SA as Server worker<br/>lanlink-‹id› (Alice)
    participant SB as Server worker<br/>lanlink-‹id› (Bob)
    participant BR as Bob<br/>lanlink-client-reader
    participant BM as Bob main<br/>thread

    Note over AR,BM: Start: Alice sent FILE_OFFER and the server forwarded it to Bob<br/>(TransferSession OFFERED, see Figure 7)

    alt Bob rejects the offer
        Note over BM: /reject ‹id› [reason]<br/>reject_file: no<br/>Receiver, no .part
        BM->>SB: FILE_REJECT (transfer_id, reason)
        Note over SA,SB: REJECTED,<br/>session deleted
        SB->>AR: FILE_REJECT
        SB->>BR: FILE_REJECT echo
        BR->>BM: event
        Note over AR: SendSession<br/>REJECTED<br/>(REJECTED_BY_PEER)
        Note over AR,AS: no sender thread was started
    else sender cancels during the chunk loop
        Note over AS: iter_chunks raises<br/>TransferError, e.g.<br/>SOURCE_CHANGED (file<br/>modified while sent).<br/>SendSession FAILED
        AS->>SA: FILE_CANCEL<br/>(transfer_id,<br/>reason)
        Note over SA,SB: CANCELLED,<br/>session deleted
        SA->>BR: FILE_CANCEL (reason)
        Note over BR: Receiver:<br/>_fail_and_cleanup<br/>deletes .part,<br/>CANCELLED<br/>(CANCELLED_BY_PEER)
        BR->>BM: final snapshot
    end

    Note over AR,BM: The CLI has no cancel command. SendSession.cancel() and Receiver.cancel()<br/>exist but nothing calls them, so FILE_CANCEL is only sent by<br/>SendSession.outgoing() after a local read error.
